  <revision rev="10" vrev="1">
    <srcmd5>c1623a954c9573b617ed4d477126962b</srcmd5>
    <version>20.0.1</version>
    <time>1793005175</time>
    <user>dimstar_suse</user>
    <comment>- Update to version 20.0.1:
  * Fix YOLO loss gradient for bounding box x/y coordinates.
  * Fix crash when reading very large images from a 32-bit
    width-step overflow.
  * Support the FFmpeg 7.1 API.
  * full_object_detection: accept parts as vector of dpoint.
  * Python: account for changed refcounting in Python 3.14,
    support functools.partial and other callables, accept CMake
    args as environment variables for setup.
  * Improve batch normalization numerical stability on CPUs and
    cuDNN convolution precision on Ampere and newer GPUs.
  * Add Adaptive Computation Time (ACT) layer and ARC-AGI dataset
    loader.
  * Build: use FindCUDAToolkit instead of deprecated FindCUDA,
    fix C++23 and gcc 16 build issues.
  * CVE-2026-24799 (boo#1257318): the bundled zlib copy is not
    affected, the inflate() extra-field guard from
    gh#davisking/dlib#3063 shipped since 19.24.9.
- Drop support-python-3.14.patch (fixed upstream).
- Fix the Python wheel build with the new toolchain:
  * pass the setup.py --no options as separate --global-option
    settings (one value per setting),
  * parse them at import time again via
    restore-module-level-arg-scan.patch (as in 20.0),
  * skip python-build's dependency check (-x) and require
    python-packaging, since the build uses the system cmake
    rather than the pip cmake module.
- Rename the shared-library subpackage to libdlib20_0_1 to match
  the libdlib.so.20.0.1 SONAME (shlib policy).
- Drop redundant -L/usr/lib64 entries from dlib-1.pc
  (pkgconfig-invalid-libs-dir).
</comment>
    <requestid>1392337</requestid>
  </revision>
</revisionlist>
